+Various heuristics assist in determining whether colors should be enabled by default. Specifically, Loguru honors |the-no-color-environment-variable|_ and disables coloring if it is set to any value. Conversely, it honors |the-force-color-environment-variable|_ and enables coloring if it is set to any value, even if the stream is not connected to a terminal. If both are set, ``NO_COLOR`` takes precedence. Additionally, terminals identified by ``TERM=dumb`` are considered to lack color support (unless ``FORCE_COLOR`` is set).
 
 In any case, you can always control log coloring by explicitly specifying the ``colorize`` argument of the |add| method::
 
